# EAS Build resolves the project root as this repo's git top-level
# directory -- a monorepo with several unrelated sub-projects (backend/,
# dashboard/, vendor-dashboard/, whuzpay-pg/, mobile/) -- even though
# `eas build` is run from inside mobile/ per Expo's own monorepo guide
# (https://docs.expo.dev/build-reference/build-with-monorepos). Presence
# of this file makes EAS ignore ALL .gitignore files repo-wide (see EAS
# CLI docs), so exclusions are written fresh here, not inherited.
#
# Exclude everything, then whitelist only mobile/ -- the one sub-project
# this build needs. This is also what fixes the original failure: EAS
# tried to copy whuzpay-pg/.codegraph/daemon.sock (a live Unix socket
# from an unrelated local tool), which a plain file copy cannot handle.
/*
!/mobile

# Generated native folders inside mobile/ must stay excluded so EAS runs
# its own `expo prebuild` from app.config.ts (managed/CNG workflow) --
# not whatever variant happens to be regenerated locally on this laptop
# at the time of upload, which would silently bypass app.config.ts
# entirely (same reasoning as mobile/.gitignore's own `/android`/`/ios`).
/mobile/android
/mobile/ios
/mobile/.expo
/mobile/node_modules
/mobile/modules/*/android/build
/mobile/modules/*/android/.gradle
